WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:03.640
Boxing has massively helped
my mental health.

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:05.000
Most of the people here

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:07.520
probably wouldn’t even have jobs
if they didn’t go here

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:10.160
because they wouldn’t
have the right state of mind.

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:12.320
It helps create that
sense of belonging.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:14.400
Without it, I don’t know
where I would be

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:35.840
Taking part
in any physical activity regularly

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:40.160
will positively impact on a person’s
physical and mental wellbeing.

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:42.920
Boxing has really high
physical demands,

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:46.920
so if a young person engages in
boxing training on a regular basis

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:48.320
and they put the effort in,

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:51.400
they’ll probably see improved
muscular strength,

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:53.160
improved muscular power

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:55.800
and improvements
in their anaerobic fitness.

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:05.320
Boxing has massively disciplined me,

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:10.560
I’ve lost 10 kilos in weight, I’ve
been eating healthy, I haven’t drunk.

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:16.560
Boxing keeps me focused,

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:19.680
it keeps me fit, it keeps me healthy,
body and mind.

00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:24.200
Boxing can also alleviate some of the
symptoms of anxiety and depression.

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:30.880
The Bulldogs is a boxing gym
based in Port Talbot.

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:33.200
We’re here to support
the local community.

00:01:42.177 --> 00:01:45.337
We’ve got people from all
walks of life, different backgrounds,

00:01:45.337 --> 00:01:48.607
we’ve got people who
are disengaged with society,

00:01:48.607 --> 00:01:50.600
some people who
are disengaged with school,

00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:53.559
and some people who have been
on the wrong side of the law.

00:01:53.559 --> 00:01:56.033
It helps create a sense of identity

00:01:56.033 --> 00:01:56.984
though attending a gym

00:01:56.984 --> 00:01:58.400
and training with others,

00:01:58.405 --> 00:02:02.685
and overall it helps create
that sense of belonging.

00:02:05.095 --> 00:02:07.090
The benefits of boxing
incorporate things

00:02:07.622 --> 00:02:10.022
such as co-operation
and teamwork.

00:02:10.022 --> 00:02:12.680
Even though boxing
may seem an individual sport,

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:16.760
it very much involves working
with a coach or a group of coaches

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:19.080
as well as other people
within a gym.

00:02:19.786 --> 00:02:23.586
And ultimately it’s really a place to
re-instil some discipline into them,

00:02:23.586 --> 00:02:26.000
and put them back
on the straight and narrow.

00:02:30.396 --> 00:02:31.836
I’ve lived in Port Talbot
my whole life.

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:35.240
There’s a lot of misconceptions
about Port Talbot,

00:02:35.240 --> 00:02:38.400
they talk about the steelworks,
or the air, or this, or that,

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:40.120
there’s not much opportunity here.

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:43.960
But there’s a lot of talent,
there's a lot of sport,

00:02:44.388 --> 00:02:47.148
and there is a sense
of community here.

00:02:49.482 --> 00:02:51.454
What happens with most boys,
what happened to me,

00:02:51.459 --> 00:02:55.579
16, 17, I got in with the
wrong crowd, started drinking,

00:02:55.584 --> 00:02:58.304
started doing this and that,
I sort of lost my way.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:03.640
I see some of the issues with Sam
as being like I see myself in him,

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:06.880
struggling, really,
for somewhere to go,

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:09.302
somewhere to see, and probably
somewhere to feel accepted.

00:03:18.610 --> 00:03:23.050
So it’s very important to be able to
build and gain the trust and respect

00:03:23.050 --> 00:03:24.800
of the young individuals
who come here.

00:03:25.099 --> 00:03:26.619
It’s about being available,

00:03:26.619 --> 00:03:29.948
it’s about mentoring,
coaching, empowering,

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:32.080
and also developing their needs,

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:34.160
because a lot
of these young people

00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:37.553
haven’t actually been able
to trust people before.

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:42.040
We all respect the coaches,
because we want them to coach us,

00:03:42.113 --> 00:03:46.593
and not for them
to shout at us and kick us out.

00:03:48.165 --> 00:03:50.198
The people in here are like a family
that I’ve never met before.

00:03:50.913 --> 00:03:54.113
So you’re like really close to them,
no matter what,

00:03:54.231 --> 00:03:56.991
they can talk to you,
even if you’re feeling down,

00:03:57.480 --> 00:03:59.320
and they’ve always got your back.

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:09.800
Some people feel that it can actually
increase aggression and violence,

00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:12.240
but research shows that it actually
has the opposite effect,

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:14.266
so it teaches young people
to react differently

00:04:14.421 --> 00:04:17.141
in situations that would normally
trigger the anger

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:19.160
and these stress responses.

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:24.600
Obviously with a sport like boxing
there’s the risks of physical injury,

00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:28.115
particularly when you’re sparring and
particularly when you’re competing.

00:04:28.346 --> 00:04:30.786
However, one could argue
that the benefits

00:04:30.786 --> 00:04:32.720
do actually outweigh these risks.

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:42.680
Boxing has massively disciplined me,

00:04:42.680 --> 00:04:44.560
it’s made me work hard, resilient,

00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:47.600
core values you need in your life
to progress.

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:50.400
They come here,
they can speak to people,

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:52.360
they can let their frustrations go

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:56.400
and really have a different
outlook and perspective on life.

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:57.600
I feel it's very important.

00:04:58.854 --> 00:05:02.374
And that sense of identity can extend
beyond the boxing gym,

00:05:02.374 --> 00:05:06.464
so not just to the gym itself,
but also to the wider community,

00:05:06.600 --> 00:05:09.800
and the wider town, village or
society where that individual lives.

00:05:10.593 --> 00:05:14.153
The Bulldogs has given me my first
opportunity to be a leader,

00:05:14.153 --> 00:05:15.447
a teacher,

00:05:15.588 --> 00:05:21.348
and now I’m going on to finish my
degree and be a qualified teacher.

